@page
@using BhugolLab.Web.Options
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<EmailOptions> EmailOptionsAccessor
@{
    var email = EmailOptionsAccessor.Value;
    ViewData["Title"] = "privacy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What data bhugol.dev collects, why, and how long it is kept. No advertising cookies, no third-party scripts.";
}
<div class="page-narrow prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Plain language, no legalese. Last updated: TODO: date.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>This site sets <strong>no advertising or analytics cookies</strong> and loads <strong>no third-party scripts</strong>.</li>
        <li>The only personal data collected is what <strong>you type into the contact form</strong>.</li>
        <li>Traffic is measured from <strong>aggregated Cloudflare zone analytics</strong> — server-side counts, not per-visitor tracking.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <h3>Contact form</h3>
    <p>
        When you send the contact form, the following is stored in this site's database:
        your name, email address, company (optional), your message, the page and
        marketing source that led you here (UTM parameters and referrer, if present),
        and the date and time of submission.
    </p>
    <h3>Technical logs</h3>
    <p>
        Like any website, the host and Cloudflare process technical request data
        (IP address, browser type, pages requested) to serve the site and defend
        against abuse. This is standard infrastructure processing, not behavioural
        tracking.
    </p>
    <h3>Cookies</h3>
    <p>
        The only cookie this site sets is a strictly necessary session cookie for the
        password-protected admin area (<code>/admin</code>). Visitors browsing the
        public pages receive no cookies from this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it is collected</h2>
    <p>
        Contact form data is used for exactly one purpose: to reply to your inquiry and,
        if it becomes a project, to run that project. The source fields tell me which of
        my outreach efforts work, in aggregate. Nothing is sold, rented, or shared with
        advertisers — there are no advertisers.
    </p>

    <h2>Who processes the data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — DNS, CDN and DDoS protection for bhugol.dev.</li>
        <li><strong>The hosting provider</strong> — <span class="todo">TODO: hosting target (e.g. Azure App Service, region)</span>, runs the site and its database.</li>
        <li><strong>The email provider</strong> — <span class="todo">TODO: SMTP/Resend provider once configured</span>, delivers your message as an email notification.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <p>
        Contact form submissions are kept for <span class="todo">TODO: retention period,
        e.g. 24 months</span> after the last reply, then deleted. Technical logs follow
        the host's and Cloudflare's default retention.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        You can ask what is stored about you, request a copy, or request deletion at any
        time. Email
        @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(email.ToAddress))
        {
            <span class="todo">TODO: contact email address</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <a href="mailto:@email.ToAddress">@email.ToAddress</a>
        }
        and I will respond within 30 days.
    </p>
</div>
